    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22908" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-dŭbĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not doubtful</i>, <i>certain</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">innocentia plurimorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 14, 45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exempla,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 5, 13, 24</span></i>
			.— Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indŭbĭē</span></b> , <i>doubtlessly</i>, <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Fragm. in
				Auct. Class. Tom. 3, 355</span></i> Mai.</div>
